summary:
  "radio", "raadio" or "fm" anywhere in a word makes the segment a station's name.

history:
  The word has to end in one, as Kaaosradio and 181.fm do. Anywhere in it,
  and a station saved as "Radiohead" or "Wolfmother" would cut the band off
  its own song.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TrackLogic.js

find:
          return /(?:radio|raadio|fm)$/.test(w) || w === "24h" || w === "247";

replace:
          return /(?:radio|raadio|fm)/.test(w) || w === "24h" || w === "247";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_tracklogic.qml::test_a_station_word_has_to_end_its_word.
  Line-neutral.
